# Rule: Lint-on-Edit Hook

If your project has **Docker** and a **Makefile**, install the lint-on-edit hook.

## What it provides

1. `hooks/lint-on-edit.sh` — single hook for Claude (`PostToolUse`) and Cursor (`afterFileEdit`).
2. `scripts/lint-route.sh` — dispatches `make lint FILE=…` to `make lint-<ext>` by extension.
3. Per-extension sub-targets (`lint-md`, `lint-ts`, `lint-sh`, …) — Dockerised linters.

## When to install

- Any project on the `makefile-conventions` baseline (Docker-first, `make up`/`test`/`down`).
- Projects where an AI agent performs repeated file edits (the feedback loop eliminates silent violations).

## When NOT to install

- Projects without Docker (the sub-targets assume container execution).
- Ephemeral CI-only environments where linting runs as a separate job.
- Projects where lint latency > 5 s P95 warm would break the editing loop (set `LINT_ON_EDIT=0`).

## Three layers — each independently testable

```
hooks/lint-on-edit.sh          ← Layer 1: trigger (no linting logic)
        │ make lint FILE=…
        ▼
scripts/lint-route.sh           ← Layer 2: router (extension → sub-target)
        │ exec make lint-<ext>
        ▼
Makefile lint-<ext> targets     ← Layer 3: per-language Dockerised linter
```

## Exit-code contract (Makefile → hook)

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `0`  | Lint passed — hook is silent |
| `1`  | Lint violations — hook sends diagnostic to agent |
| `64` | Policy gap — extension declared in neither LINT_ROUTES nor LINT_IGNORED |
| `65` | Wiring missing — linter binary absent or service down |
| `124`| Timeout — hook kills make and sends timeout message |

## Key env knobs

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `LINT_ON_EDIT` | `1` | Set to `0` to disable globally |
| `LINT_TIMEOUT` | `120` | Seconds before killing make |
| `LINT_HOOK_HOST` | (sniffed) | `claude` or `cursor` |
| `LINT_DEBUG` | `0` | Set to `1` for verbose logging |

